# Global Governance

- Production-ready, enterprise-grade output only — no quick workarounds.
- Prefer clear, testable code over clever shortcuts.
- Enforce modular boundaries; use domain language from the approved glossary.
- Capture assumptions, open questions, and risks explicitly in audits and harness.
- Register remaining gaps as Open DQ with owner when requirements are ambiguous; do not invent. Do not STOP for a clarification round except human gates.
